From bb580b6370405588b03ebea4858bd8fcb3da914e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:55:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper_inject: never inject on an AiMesh node - it loops the
 UI to a blank page

Field report: flashing a NODE leaves its web UI a blank page whose URL cycles,
with no way to reach the login page. Distinct from the factory-reset first-boot
loop fixed in v2.2.0 (137d96338a) - different root cause, and this one only
fires when the box is an AiMesh node.

On a node httpd locks the UI down to a whitelist (httpd.c, the RTCONFIG_AMAS
branch): with re_mode=1 (or disable_ui=1) and re_upgrade=0, every page outside
AiMesh_whitelists[] (web.c) is answered with a meta-refresh to message.htm
instead of the page. That check runs BEFORE auth_check, which is why the login
page was never reached either.

message.htm IS whitelisted, is served text/html through do_ej, and was not
skip-listed here - so it took the normal bounce and replaced the top window
with /reaper_shell.asp. The shell is NOT whitelisted; no Reaper page is, the
list is stock ASUS. So httpd meta-refreshed it straight back to message.htm,
which bounced again. message.htm <-> reaper_shell.asp with no exit. The
injected block sits before </head>, so location.replace() ran during head parse
and the body never painted: blank page, cycling URL bar.

AiMesh_Node_FirmwareUpgrade.asp is whitelisted but equally unlisted here, so a
node in this state could not even be re-flashed through its own UI.

A node has no Reaper UI to reach in ANY state - shell, dashboard, first-boot
gate and every native page are outside the whitelist by construction. Serve
pristine stock instead, which is what an AiMesh node is meant to show.

Deliberately NOT gated on re_upgrade, unlike httpd's own lockdown test. During
a node upgrade httpd opens the whitelist back up, so the bounce would stop
looping - but it would then swallow AiMesh_Node_FirmwareUpgrade.asp /
Updating.asp into the shell iframe, where the progress page is not meant to
live. No node state wants the bounce, so the guard is unconditional.

Spelled with nvram_get()/nvram_match() rather than nvram_get_int(): the latter
lives in shared.h, which this file deliberately does not pull in.

Affects every model identically - sibling port owed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c b/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
index 994ca27fb4..3bec66685a 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
@@ -253,6 +253,36 @@ static int reaper_should_inject(struct mime_handler *h, const char *file)
 	if (v && *v && atoi(v) == 0)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* reaper 2026-08-17 field fix: "flashing a NODE gives a blank page whose URL
+	 * loops". On an AiMesh node httpd locks the web UI down to a whitelist
+	 * (httpd.c, the RTCONFIG_AMAS branch): with re_mode=1 (or disable_ui=1) and
+	 * re_upgrade=0, EVERY page outside AiMesh_whitelists[] (web.c) is answered
+	 * with "<meta http-equiv=refresh url=message.htm>" instead of the page.
+	 *
+	 * message.htm IS whitelisted, is served text/html through do_ej, and was not
+	 * skip-listed here - so it took the normal bounce and replaced the top window
+	 * with /reaper_shell.asp. The shell is NOT whitelisted (no Reaper page is),
+	 * so httpd meta-refreshed it straight back to message.htm, which bounced
+	 * again: message.htm <-> reaper_shell.asp with no exit. The injected block
+	 * sits before </head>, so location.replace() ran during head parse and the
+	 * body never painted - a blank page with a cycling URL bar, and no way to
+	 * reach the login page, which is exactly the field report.
+	 *
+	 * A node has no Reaper UI to reach in ANY state: the shell, the dashboard,
+	 * the first-boot gate and every native page are outside the whitelist by
+	 * construction. So there is nothing to inject and nowhere to bounce to -
+	 * serve pristine stock, which is what an AiMesh node is meant to show.
+	 *
+	 * Deliberately NOT gated on re_upgrade, unlike httpd's own lockdown test.
+	 * While a node upgrade is running httpd opens the whitelist back up, so the
+	 * bounce would stop looping - but it would then swallow
+	 * AiMesh_Node_FirmwareUpgrade.asp / Updating.asp into the shell iframe,
+	 * where the progress page is not meant to live. There is no node state in
+	 * which bouncing into the Reaper shell is the right answer, so the guard is
+	 * unconditional. */
+	if (nvram_match("re_mode", "1") || nvram_match("disable_ui", "1"))
+		return 0;
+
 	/* only text/html; this alone excludes state.js, **.js/json/xml/css */
 	if (!h || !h->mime_type || strncasecmp(h->mime_type, "text/html", 9) != 0)
 		return 0;
